# To test any of these, just copy one block 
# and paste it into 'test.flow' to see how the compiler handles it!

# ------------------------------------------
# THE ULTIMATE EXAMPLE (All Features Combined)
# ------------------------------------------
# This script has no errors and is perfect for showing off!
# It perfectly demonstrates:
# 1. Case Insensitivity (sEt, fOr, bEgIn)
# 2. Constant Folding (10 * 5 squashes to 50)
# 3. Dead-Copy Elimination (t1 disappears completely)
# 4. TAC Loop Flattening (The FOR loop flattens to JZ/GOTO)
# 5. Semantic Type Inference (Symbol table detects 'int' and 'string')

sEt baseScore tO 10 * 5
SET total TO baseScore

fOr i fRoM 1 tO 3 Do bEgIn
    SET total TO total + 10
eNd

IF total > 40 tHeN BeGiN
    priNT "The final optimized score is:"
    pRiNt total
EnD

# ------------------------------------------
# 1. THE OPTIMIZER (Constant Folding)
# ------------------------------------------
# The compiler will calculate "10 * 5" during Phase 5 (Optimized TAC)
# so the final Assembly code will just say: LOAD 50.
SET score TO 10 * 5
PRINT score

# ------------------------------------------
# 2. THE OPTIMIZER (Dead-Copy Elimination)
# ------------------------------------------
# When doing math, Phase 4 generates messy middle-men (e.g. t1 = 50 + 50, health = t1).
# Phase 5 folds the math (t1 = 100) and then eliminates the dead copy (health = 100)!
SET health TO 50 + 50
PRINT health

# ------------------------------------------
# 3. SYNTAX ERROR (Phase 2 - Parser Error)
# ------------------------------------------
# Uncomment the line below to crash the Parser! 
# We forgot the "TO" keyword. The parser will yell: "Expected 'TO' but got '99'"
# SET errorVar 99

# ------------------------------------------
# 4. SEMANTIC ERROR (Phase 3 - Logic Error)
# ------------------------------------------
# Uncomment the line below to crash the Semantic Analyzer!
# We are trying to print a variable that hasn't been assigned yet.
# It will say "Variable 'missingVar' used before assignment"
# PRINT missingVar

# ------------------------------------------
# 5. FLATTENING LOOPS (Phase 4 - TAC Generation)
# ------------------------------------------
# This shows off how beautifully the compiler flattens a nested loop
# into linear GOTO jumps. Look at the Phase 4 output for this!
SET total TO 0
FOR i FROM 1 TO 3 DO BEGIN
    SET total TO total + i
END
PRINT "Total is: " + total

# ------------------------------------------
# 6. CASE INSENSITIVE LEXER (Phase 1)
# ------------------------------------------
# The Lexer allows any capitalization for keywords, but variables are strict!
sEt myVar to 10
If myVar == 10 tHeN BeGiN
    priNT "Case Insensitivity works!"
EnD
